---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import hero from '../../../assets/screenshots/hero.png';
import '../styles/home.css';

const features = [
  { title: 'Always on', copy: 'Close the window or disconnect. The Server and your agents keep working.' },
  { title: 'Remote access', copy: 'Manage local and remote devices in one window, over SSH, TCP or Peer-to-peer.' },
  { title: 'Agent status', copy: 'The sidebar shows what each agent is doing. Condr notifies you when an agent finishes.' },
  { title: 'Agent driven', copy: 'Agents can use Condr too: create panes, read output, assign tasks, and talk to other agents.' },
  { title: 'Real terminals', copy: 'Every pane is a real terminal built on the alacritty core. Run any CLI agent or terminal program.' },
  { title: 'Fast', copy: 'Written entirely in Rust, with no Electron. Small and responsive, even while agents are busy.' },
];

const releases = 'https://github.com/condrdev/condr/releases';
const github = 'https://github.com/condrdev/condr';

const agents = [
  { name: 'Claude Code', icon: 'claude' },
  { name: 'Codex', icon: 'codex' },
  { name: 'OpenCode', icon: 'opencode' },
  { name: 'Pi', icon: 'pi' },
  { name: 'OMP', icon: 'omp' },
  { name: 'Antigravity', icon: 'antigravity' },
  { name: 'Grok', icon: 'grok' },
  { name: 'Cursor', icon: 'cursor' },
  { name: 'Copilot', icon: 'copilot' },
  { name: 'Kimi', icon: 'kimi' },
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Condr keeps your agents running. One window for all your agents, local or remote." />
    <link rel="icon" href="/condr.svg" />
    <title>Condr — Keep your agents running</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="ambient ambient-one" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="ambient ambient-two" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <header class="site-header shell">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Condr home"><img src="/condr.svg" alt="" /><span>Condr</span></a>
      <div class="header-actions">
        <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
          <a href={github}>GitHub</a>
        </nav>
        <a class="header-button" href={releases}>Download</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero shell">
        <h1>Keep your agents<br /><span>running.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">One window for all your agents.<br />Local or remote, step away and pick up where you left off.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={releases}>Download</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Get started <span>→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-meta"><span>Windows</span><i></i><span>macOS</span><i></i><span>Linux</span><i></i><span>Built in Rust</span></div>
      </section>

      <section class="product-shot shell" aria-label="Condr workspace screenshot">
        <div class="shot-halo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <figure><Image src={hero} alt="Condr connected to local and remote Servers, with Claude Code and Codex running side by side in each Workspace" loading="eager" widths={[640, 960, 1280, hero.width]} sizes="(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" /><figcaption><span>One workspace</span><span>Claude Code · Codex · any CLI</span></figcaption></figure>
        <div class="agent-strip" aria-label="Supported agent CLIs">
          {agents.map((agent) => <span class="agent-item"><img src={`/agents/${agent.icon}.svg`} alt="" aria-hidden="true" />{agent.name}</span>)}
          <span class="agent-more">and more</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="features shell" id="features">
        <div class="statement">
          <p class="section-label">Everything in one window</p>
          <h2>Give every agent a place<br /><span>to work.</span></h2>
          <p class="statement-copy">Condr is a small desktop app. It runs Claude Code, Codex, and other CLI agents in one window, along with any other terminal program. Each agent gets a real terminal. You get one clear view.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          {features.map((feature) => (
            <article class="feature-card"><h3>{feature.title}</h3><p>{feature.copy}</p></article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="remote shell" id="remote">
        <div class="remote-copy"><div class="section-label">Local or remote</div><h2>Leave the machine.<br /><span>Keep the work.</span></h2><p>Install the headless Server on any device, then connect from your desktop over SSH, pair over TCP with a one-time link, or go Peer-to-peer when both machines sit behind NAT: no fixed IP needed, no VPN to install. Every way gives you the same window and the same workspaces.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/getting-started/#connect-to-a-remote-device">How to connect a remote device <span>→</span></a></div>
        <div class="connection-card">
          <div class="connection-head"><span class="connection-live"></span><span>Remote connections</span><span class="connection-count">SSH · TCP · P2P</span></div>
          <div class="remote-method">
            <div class="method-icon">↗</div>
            <strong>SSH</strong>
            <small class="method-description">Uses your OpenSSH configuration and ssh-agent.</small>
          </div>
          <code class="remote-code">ssh://user@build-box</code>
          <div class="remote-method">
            <div class="method-icon method-tcp">⌁</div>
            <strong>TCP pairing</strong>
            <small class="method-description">Pairing link from <code>condr server invite</code>.</small>
          </div>
          <code class="remote-code">tcp://&lt;server key&gt;.&lt;invite&gt;@&lt;host&gt;:&lt;port&gt;</code>
          <div class="remote-method">
            <div class="method-icon method-p2p">⟷</div>
            <strong>Peer-to-peer</strong>
            <small class="method-description">Both behind NAT. End-to-end encrypted over <a href="https://www.iroh.computer/">iroh</a>; the relay never sees what you send.</small>
          </div>
          <code class="remote-code">p2p://&lt;server key&gt;.&lt;invite&gt;</code>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer shell"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Condr home"><img src="/condr.svg" alt="" /><span>Condr</span></a><span>Keep your agents running.</span><div><a href="/docs/">Docs</a> <a href={github}>GitHub</a></div></footer>
  </body>
</html>
